---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/telehealth-for-therapists/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="ed-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">Mental health EHR</a>{" "}
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">
          Telehealth for Therapists &amp; Mental Health Practices
        </span>
      </nav>
      <div class="ed-feature-hero">
        <section class="ed-hero">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Telehealth for mental health</div>
            <h1>
              Meet your client.
              <br />
              <em>Keep the context close.</em>
            </h1>
            <p class="ed-dek">
              Otto brings video visits into the same workspace as session
              preparation, clinical notes, and the patient record. Move through
              the encounter with the information you need nearby.
            </p>
            <div class="ed-actions">
              <a class="button" href="/waitlist/">
                Join the waitlist ↗
              </a>
              <a class="text-link" href="/demo/#watch">
                Watch the 2-minute demo ↗
              </a>
            </div>
            <p class="micro">
              For independent mental health practices · Built by Tebra
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ed-hero-art">
            <img
              class="ed-photo"
              src="/assets/therapist-session.png"
              alt="A therapist listening during a client session"
              width="640"
              height="420"
            />
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">The work, connected</span>
            <h2>One workspace, from preparation to follow-through.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            A video visit is part of a longer care relationship. Connect the
            appointment with the work that comes before and after it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>Prepare before joining</h3>
            <p>
              Review the patient summary and last-session highlights while
              getting ready for the conversation.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>Meet inside Otto</h3>
            <p>
              Use the waiting room, prejoin audio and video checks, and split
              visit layout described in Otto’s telehealth experience.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Continue into documentation</h3>
            <p>
              With appropriate consent, capture audio for the note. Review the
              draft, sign, and confirm proposed chart updates.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-story">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Inside the workflow</span>
          <h2>Keep the visit and the record together.</h2>
          <p>
            Integrated telehealth keeps the encounter within Otto’s practice
            workflow. Review the client context, meet, then continue into
            documentation and payment without assembling a separate process for
            every stage.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/demo/#watch">
            See the complete visit ↗
          </a>
        </div>
        <ul class="ed-checks">
          <li>Secure join links and patient verification</li>
          <li>A provider meeting room and waiting room</li>
          <li>Prejoin checks for audio and video</li>
          <li>A split visit layout inside the workspace</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-faq">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</span>
          <h2>Get to know the details.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Do I need a separate video application?</summary>
            <p>
              Otto describes integrated telehealth inside its provider
              workspace. Confirm supported browsers, devices, and patient join
              requirements during setup.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I use Otto for in-person visits too?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. The documentation and patient-record workflows also apply to
              in-person sessions. Patient consent is still needed when recording
              audio.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are group or couples sessions supported?</summary>
            <p>
              Confirm your exact visit type with the team. This preview does not
              establish support for group, couples, or multi-party telehealth.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Where can I review privacy and recording terms?</summary>
            <p>
              Start with <a href="/security/">security and data questions</a>,
              then request the applicable written terms from Otto.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</span>
        <div class="ed-resources">
          <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">The mental health EHR ↗</a>
          <a href="/ai-progress-notes/">AI progress notes ↗</a>
          <a href="/compare/">Compare your options ↗</a>
          <a href="/tools/">Free practice tools ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-close">
        <div>
          <h2>See what a connected practice day can feel like.</h2>
          <p>
            Watch Otto carry a visit from preparation through documentation and
            payment. Then tell us about the way you practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
          Join the waitlist ↗
        </a>
      </section>
      <p class="ed-source">
        Product details checked against{" "}
        <a href="https://otto.tebra.com/">Otto’s public website</a> on October
        16, 2026. Confirm availability and service terms for your practice.
        Workflow examples are illustrative and use fictional information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
